Subject: [PATCH 18/18] x86+amd64: the VGA FCode blob was defined into the root node

The bug patches 14 and 16 fixed in C, a third time, in Forth -- and this one had
been shipping on x86 for years with CONFIG_DRIVER_VGA set to TRUE.

arch/{x86,amd64}/init.fs line 9 executes

    " /" find-device

and nothing ever closes it. Eighty lines later the file does

    [IFDEF] CONFIG_DRIVER_VGA
      -1 value vga-driver-fcode
      " QEMU,VGA.bin" $encode-file to vga-driver-fcode
    [THEN]

`value` is $create, and $create defines into the CURRENT VOCABULARY. So
vga-driver-fcode was created as a method of the ROOT NODE, not as a dictionary
word. Measured at the x86 prompt before this patch:

    0 > " vga-driver-fcode" $find .
    0                                    \ not found
    0 > vga-driver-fcode u.
    vga-driver-fcode: undefined word.
    0 > dev / " vga-driver-fcode" $find .
    -1                                   \ found -- inside root
    0 > dev / words
    vga-driver-fcode preopen make-openable encode-unit decode-unit close open

drivers/pci.c:1045 runs

    feval("['] vga-driver-fcode 2 cells + 1 byte-load")

from vga_config_cb, with the PCI DEVICE node current -- not root -- so the
lookup failed on every boot and the FCode driver has never been evaluated on
either arch.

WHAT THE FAILURE LOOKED LIKE, and why it survived: forth/bootstrap/interpreter.fs:64
reports an unresolvable token with

    type 3a emit

-- the word, then a colon -- and then throws -13. feval's caller prints no
status, so the entire failure is the string

    vga-driver-fcode:

with no newline, no "undefined word", and the next printk landing on the same
line. It reads as a progress marker. This lab had already written that exact
string into drivers/floppy.c as a boot LANDMARK ("hung ... right after
`vga-driver-fcode:`"), which is how thoroughly it passes for normal output.

WHY IT SURVIVED UPSTREAM: arch/ppc/ppc.fs carries the same block and never calls
find-device, so on ppc the word is global and the driver has always loaded.
Verified, unchanged by this patch:

    ppc     0 > " vga-driver-fcode" $find .   ->  -1     (before and after)

It is broken only on the two arches nobody boots.

THE FIX is one word: device-end, before the block. Measured after, on both:

                                       x86              amd64
  " vga-driver-fcode" $find .          -1  (was 0)      -1  (was 0)
  "vga-driver-fcode:" in the boot log  gone             gone
  openbios-video-width                 320              320  (was 0)
  QEMU,VGA@0 under the host bridge     present          present (new, patch 17)

NOT closed by this patch: `" screen" find-dev` still returns 0 on both arches
-- there is no screen devalias, so a display node exists and nothing points at
it. That is a separate question and is recorded as one, not folded into this
result.

All eleven smoke tracks pass on x86, amd64 and ppc after this patch. It is
confined to arch/{x86,amd64}/ and needs no Arch-tested: line; ppc was built and
driven anyway, because it is the control that explains the bug.

--- a/arch/x86/init.fs
+++ b/arch/x86/init.fs
@@ -91,7 +91,31 @@
 ; CONSOLE-IN-initializer
 
 \ Load VGA FCode driver blob
+\
+\ device-end FIRST, and it is load-bearing. Line 9 of this file executes
+\ `" /" find-device` and NOTHING closes it, so everything below runs with the
+\ ROOT NODE as the current device -- and `value` is $create, which defines into
+\ the CURRENT VOCABULARY. Without this, `vga-driver-fcode` lands in root's
+\ method list instead of the dictionary: measured on x86, `dev / words` prints
+\ it, a bare `$find` returns 0, and drivers/pci.c:1045's
+\ `feval("['] vga-driver-fcode 2 cells + 1 byte-load")` -- which runs with the
+\ PCI device node current, not root -- reported it undefined every boot.
+\
+\ The report is one token long and looks like progress: interpreter.fs:64 does
+\ `type 3a emit` (the word, then a colon) before throwing -13, and feval's
+\ caller prints no status, so the whole failure is the string
+\ "vga-driver-fcode:" with no newline. This lab had already written that string
+\ into drivers/floppy.c as a boot LANDMARK. The FCode driver has never been
+\ evaluated on x86 or amd64.
+\
+\ arch/ppc/ppc.fs carries the same block and never calls find-device, so ppc's
+\ copy is a global word and ppc's VGA has always worked -- which is why this
+\ survived: it is broken only on the arches nobody boots.
+\
+\ Same defect as patches 14 and 16 (bind_func before device_end), third
+\ instance, this time in Forth rather than C.
 [IFDEF] CONFIG_DRIVER_VGA
+  device-end
   -1 value vga-driver-fcode
   " QEMU,VGA.bin" $encode-file to vga-driver-fcode
 [THEN]
--- a/arch/amd64/init.fs
+++ b/arch/amd64/init.fs
@@ -90,7 +90,31 @@
